<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">How we examine planning applications</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">An Inspector or appointed person examines the application and makes the final decision.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">They will decide whether to examine the application using one of two procedure types:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
	<li><strong class="govuk-!-font-weight-bold">written representations</strong> (reviewing written comments and supporting attachments)</li>
	<li><strong class="govuk-!-font-weight-bold">hearing</strong> (a meeting led by the Inspector or appointed person)</li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">We will notify you about the chosen procedure if you are:</p>
<ul class='govuk-list govuk-list--bullet'>
	<li>the applicant</li>
	<li>the local planning authority</li>
	<li>anyone who submitted a comment</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Changes to the process</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">	We can change how an application is examined at any time before making a final decision.</p>
